    "durationMs": 189143,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and verified. Here's what I built:\n\n**Stack**: Laravel 11 (v11.57.1) on PHP 8.3, Eloquent + MySQL via the provided `DB_*` environment variables (I stripped DB settings from `.env` so nothing is hard-coded).\n\n**Endpoints** (registered in `routes/api.php` with `apiPrefix: ''` in `bootstrap/app.php`, so paths are `/links` and `/r/{code}`):\n- `POST /links` — validates `url` (absolute http/https with host, via a `parse_url`-based rule) and optional `code` (`^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$`); auto-generates 8-char alphanumeric codes with uniqueness retry; returns 201 `{code, url, clicks: 0}` with the URL unchanged; duplicate code → 409 with `error`\n- `GET /links/{code}` — 200 with `{code, url, clicks}` or 404 with `error`\n- `GET /r/{code}` — 302 with correct `Location`, increments clicks atomically via `increment()`; unknown → 404 with `error`\n- `GET /links` — `{items: [...], total}` in ascending creation order\n- All 422s (malformed JSON, missing/invalid url, invalid code) return JSON with an `error` field — I used `shouldRenderJsonWhen` plus a `ValidationException` renderer so JSON is returned even without an `Accept` header\n\n**Verified with 20 curl checks**, then a restart test: clicks continued from 3 → 4 across a server restart, confirming persistence. Also ran the default test suite (2 passed) and a final clean boot of `start.sh`.\n\n**Ops**: `start.sh` is executable and runs `php artisan migrate --force` then `exec php artisan serve --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8000 --no-reload` (deps were installed with Composer ahead of time, not in the script). README documents startup and the API. The server is stopped, port 8000 is free, and the links table is empty for the graded run."
